Has any performance testing been done between the DE500/DE504 DEC
10/100 NICs and the current Intel DE600 NICs, specifically for use in
OpenVMS Alpha systems?  I've got a customer who replaced a DE500-BA
with a DE600 in an ES40 (quad CPU) system after an unfortunate cable
trip physically damaged the old card (and fortunately nothing else). 
They are complaining about a slight but measurable performance
decrease for remote clients with a slight but measurable decrease in
CPU usage for their current load.

There is not a really solid baseline here; their tools don't track
overall system or network load, so there could easily have been
unrelated factors causing the measurement changes (like users being
less frenetic,
different overall network utilization, etc), but it'd be interesting
to find out.  If it comes down to it I have a few DE500-BAs set aside
for future replacement needs and can substitute one.

Any info appreciated.

