OpenVMS DECwindows Motif Server Mandatory Update Patch
Frequently Asked Questions
29-October-2001


Q.  Why is Compaq issuing this Mandatory Update Patch (MUP) for OpenVMS?

	This Mandatory Update Patch is being issued in response to a
recent problem report on systems running OpenVMS Alpha, OpenVMS VAX,
SEVMS VAX or SEVMS Alpha with the DECwindows Motif Server installed.
These systems have a potential security vulnerability that could be
exploited to allow existing users unauthorized access to data and system
resources.

Q.  What versions of OpenVMS are impacted?

	All supported versions of OpenVMS Alpha, OpenVMS VAX, SEVMS VAX
or SEVMS Alpha have been examined for this vulnerability.  All supported
versions with the exception of OpenVMS VAX Version V5.5-2 are impacted.

	Supported Versions Impacted:
		*	OpenVMS Alpha Version 6.2 and all associated
                          hardware releases (for example, Version 6.2-1H1)
		*	OpenVMS Alpha Version 7.1-2
		*	OpenVMS Alpha Version 7.2-1H1
		*	OpenVMS Alpha Version 7.2-2
		*	OpenVMS Alpha Version 7.3
		*	OpenVMS VAX Version 6.2
		*	OpenVMS VAX Version 7.1
		*	OpenVMS VAX Version 7.2
		*	OpenVMS VAX Version 7.3
		*	SEVMS Alpha Version 6.2
		*	SEVMS VAX Version 6.2

	Supported Versions NOT Impacted:
		*	OpenVMS VAX Version 5.5-2

Q.  Do I still need the patch if I am not running the DECwindows Motif
Server on my system?

	No.  This patch is only required for systems running the
DECwindows Motif Server.  Installation of the DECwindows Motif Server is
optional during the installation of the OpenVMS Operating System.  You
may be running the DECwindows Motif Server on your system even if you
are not running the DECwindows Motif layered product.

Q.  How can I tell if I am running the DECwindows Server on my system?

	You can verify whether or not the DECwindows Motif Server has
been installed on your system by using the following command:

	             $ DIRECTORY SYS$LIBRARY:DECW$*.EXE

	If no DECW$*.EXE files are present on your system, the
DECwindows Motif Server is not installed on your system and you do not
need to apply this mandatory update.

Q.  How can I get the patch I need for my version of OpenVMS?

	There are three ways to get copies of the patches.

	1) If you have a service contract that provides media updates to
the OpenVMS Operating System or if you have purchased a media kit
containing the OpenVMS Operating System from Compaq in the past six
months, a CD-ROM containing patches for all impacted versions will
automatically be shipped to you in early November.

	2) You may download the patches from the World Wide Web at the
following address:

	             <http://www.support.compaq.com/patches>

	At the web site listed above, use the FTP access option, select
VMS then either the VAX or AXP directory, then choose the appropriate
version directory and download the patch as identified in the applicable
.HTML file accordingly.

	Note: Please review the README file(s) for each patch prior to
installation.

	The patch filenames are:

		*	OpenVMS ALPHA

				o DEC-AXPVMS-VMS73_DW_MOT_MUP-V0100-4.PCSI
				o DEC-AXPVMS-VMS722_DW_MOT_MUP-V0100-4.PCSI
				o DEC-AXPVMS-VMS721H1_DW_MOT_MUP-V0100-4.PCSI
				o DEC-AXPVMS-VMS721_DW_MOT_MUP-V0100-4.PCSI
				o DEC-AXPVMS-VMS712_DW_MOT_MUP-V0100-4.PCSI
				o ALPDWMOTMUP01_062.A

		*	OpenVMS VAX

				o VAXDWMOTMUP01_073.A
				o VAXDWMOTMUP01_072.A
				o VAXDWMOTMUP01_071.A
				o VAXDWMOTMUP01_062.A

		*	SEVMS

				o SE_VAXDWMOTMUP01_062.A
				o SE_ALPDWMOTMUP01_062.A


	3) Customers who do not automatically receive a CD-ROM and
cannot access the web site kits should contact their local Compaq Sales
Office to order a CD-ROM containing the patches.  The part number for
the CD-ROM is QA-MT3AA-T8. There will be a charge for shipping and
handling.

Q.  How can I tell if this patch has already been installed on my
system?

	For PSCI kits, use the PRODUCT SHOW HISTORY command.  For
example:

	$ PRODUCT SHOW HISTORY VMS***_MOT_MUP/VERSION=1.0

	--------------------------------------------...
	PRODUCT                                     ...
	--------------------------------------------...
	DEC AXPVMS VMS721H1_DW_MOT_MUP V1.0 Patch   ...
	--------------------------------------------...

	For VMSINSTAL kits (.A savesets) search for a .TXT file in
SYS$COMMON:[SYSUPD] that has the same name as the kit.   For example:

	$ DIR SYS$COMMON:[SYSUPD]*DWMOTMUP01*.TXT

	Directory SYS$COMMON:[SYSUPD]

	ALPDWMOTMUP01_62.TXT;1

Q.	Do I need to reboot my system after I install the patch?

	After you apply this update, you must reboot your system in
order for the changes to take effect.   If you have other nodes in your
OpenVMS cluster, they must also be rebooted in order to make use of the
new images.  If it is not possible or convenient to reboot the entire
cluster at this time, a rolling reboot may be performed.  However, due
to the nature of the problem that this kit corrects, Compaq strongly
recommends a rolling reboot be performed immediately on each cluster
node.

	Q.	Do I need to reapply the patch if I upgrade my version
of the operating system in the future?

	Yes.  If you upgrade to any of the impacted versions, you must
apply the patch appropriate to the new version of the operating system.



