You mean the potiometers/trimmers at the lower right side (screen facing
you)? The focus pot is on the left side, in a black or white 'hermtic'
plastic case, probably near the top of the aluminium cage. There might
even be two of them, Horiz. Focus and Vert. Focus.
At least they were there with a GDM 1962 from Sun.

 Now I need to adjust the focus.
> I searched on Google but haven't found much info about that.
> Any hint how to do it or a link to a online manual would be very appreciated.
> 

Use an isolated Philips screwdriver. This pot is likely sealed with
white glue/cement, so if you use the small black trimming tool you found
inside, you will likely break it...

Note that depending on the age and amount of use you will not be able to
get a sharp image anymore. Even CRTs have a limited lifetime...

