> I have just saved from the dump a Microvax 3400. I'd like to get it working
> again, but haven't really got very much knowledge about these machines. When
> I turn it on it whirs away quite happily but the front panel shows an error
> with disk 0 (an RF71). The other disk (disk1) clicks away for a few minutes
> and then stops, the numeric display on card 1 stops eventually on 3.
> 
> I presume I need to find a new disk ( does it boot of disk 0 ? ), I suppose
> what i'm really after is a FAQ to get this thing started, does anyone know
> of any such place / have any pointers on where to start ? Or is it too much
> hassle to get it fixed ?

You might get more advice in the comp.os.vms newsgroup.

See the OpenVMS FAQ.  You can find it by starting at
   www.openvms.compaq.com.

The problem _might_ be that the system can't find a disk with VMS on it. 
Some microvax system consoles attempt to boot from various devices until
it found the OS; some remember the default boot disk in non-volatile RAM. 
I'm not sure about the 3400.  The system might be trying to boot from
either of these disks, or it might be trying to boot via ethernet.

Have you found the console port, and connected a suitable terminal so you
can see messages from the system?  It will be hard to give useful advice
until you do that.

On most microvaxes, if the numeric display gets down to 3, the important
self-tests have passed, and it is trying to boot the OS.  The count won't
go down any farther unless it finds useable software.  So I suspect your
system is healthy, but the OS is missing or scrambled.

