Hi Rhys

I have a MV3400 at home, a fine machine.  When you power on the MV3400
it goes through a self test which finishes at 3  (with a serial terminal
connected to the console port you will see the count down on the
terminal),  it can then either boot automatically (2..1..0) or drop into
console mode and give you the three chevron prompt >>>.  In console mode
there is a HELP menu.

You can get a list of the disks in your system 			SHO DEVICE
You can try booting from another disk 				BOOT device  	(e.g. DIA1)
You can set the device the machine attempts to auto boot from  	SET BOOT
device

Try booting from the other disks in your system to see if there is a
system on them.

You can get the VMS FAQ which has lots of helpful info at 
http://www.openvms.compaq.com/wizard/openvms_faq.html
Also comp.os.vms is the best place to raise questions for VAX and VMS. 
Good luck

Regards, Trevor  
 

