I have an Emulex card I would like to identify.

It's a quad Qbus card with S-box mounting hardware.

The card has "ASSY QT1410402-00 REV-D" on the board and "ASSY
NO QT1410202-02 REV M" on a  sticker on a 40 pin IC.

The front panel has, from top to bottom:

   3 LED's , labeled "3 2 1"

   A 4 pole DIP switch, labeled "SW1"

  A 3 pin connector, labeled "J2"

  Two male HD-50 connectors, labeled "J1" and "J2".

The HD-50 connectors are the wrong gender to be SCSI-2 connectors, and
have the wrong mounting hardware to be DSSI connectors.
On the circuit board is a 14 pin connector labeled "J4", a 8 pole DIP
switch labeled "SW2", and next to the "A" Qbus connector a set of
jumpers labeled " D E F G H I J K".





