> I hate it when you're cryptic, Terry.  What does this mean???  Shannon may
> know, but some of the rest of us don't and when you couch things in your
> insider code like this, the rest of us just sit scratching our heads
> thinking "What the hell it that?".

It was an initiative to render Windows NT "industrial strength." It involved
the porting of the NonStop SQL/MX database to NT, the porting of the VMS
cluster file system and DLM to NT, and the porting of several other VMS
products to NT. Much of the work was actually done, but the plug was pulled
in mid-1999. Had the project gone forward Alpha would have been the
reference platform for Win64.

Shoulda, woulda, coulda, but didn't...




