:I have an RZ1CC-BA and I want to get another. This drive is made by
:Quantum. Does anybody know the quantum part number so I can
:get basically the same drive without having to pay DEC prices?

  RZ1CC-BA is a 4.3GB 7200 RPM UltraSCSI disk, which isn't the newest 
  storage technology around.  Because of its relative age (not new, but
  not old enough to be a paperweight), you might well find one of these 
  disks on the used-equipment market.
    
  Check the OpenVMS FAQ for the section discussing connecting third-party
  SCSI widgets to OpenVMS.  (While you don't mention the specific platform,
  storage mounting, and operating system -- I am assuming much here.)

  It's certainly possible and many folks have managed to connect third-party 
  SCSI disks to OpenVMS, but the success and the effort involved can and 
  does vary.  "TANSTAAFL" ("There ain't no such thing as a free lunch"), in 
  other words.  Sometimes this is easy, and sometimes it is definitely not.

  Of larger interest can be the mounting(s) involved -- since you have one 
  of these widgets already installed, I will assume the enclosure has 
  sufficient power and cooling for these disks and specifically for another
  of these disks.  (If the cooling is insufficient, then the disks do tend 
  to slowly cook themselves over time.  Failure is not immediate, too.)


