Jason,

You probably ought to download all the manuals you need.  You won't
get into trouble for doing so.

Yes, different 3.52v VRMs are required for P150, P166, P200 (single
only).  The VRM for the P133s is nothing more than a shunt that allows
3.3v to pass thru.  In this respect, the Prioris XL is just like the
Celebris XL and the big Prioris HX.  They all use the same 54-24490
processor card, the latest and last one made.

DEC was not quite unique in using Socket 5 for Pentium chips faster
than 133MHz.  Apparently, there is little difference between Socket 5
and Socket 7.  It's the circuitry on the motherboard or processor card
that makes the difference.  Supposedly, the physical Socket 7 also is
supposed to withstand better the higher current consumed by the faster
CPUs... Ben Myers

