In article <YHCv7.14914$oY4.1579571@wagner.videotron.net>, Eric LeBlanc <inouk@NOSPAM.igt.net> writes:

:I have one MicroVAX II with M7555 controler (so MFM I believe).  But, I 
:want to know if it is possible use module with SCSI for hard drives ? If 
:yes, which module? M???? :)

  M7555 is RQDX3.  No, this is not a SCSI controller.  This Q-bus widget
  is intended for use with the RD53 series disks and particularly with 
  the RD54 series disks, and uses ST506/MFM connections.

  SCSI is possible on VAX Q-bus systems, but is not particularly easy.

  If you want SCSI on a Q-bus enclosure OpenVMS VAX system, you will want 
  to acquire the KFQSA to DSSI Q-bus module, and HSD05 or HSD10 series 
  DSSI to SCSI adapter, or you will want a third-party Q-bus to SCSI 
  adapter.  (These will all be exceedingly slow, and most of these Q-bus
  configurations and these widgets will provide only SCSI-1 connections.)

  It will likely be simpler and easier to get mid- to upper-end MicroVAX 
  3100 series or a VAXstation 4000 series, and use the (far) faster VAX
  processor and the native SCSI connections that are provided on these
  and various other VAX series boxes.


