If the system boots, then you can log in as root and use consvar to change the value
of the CONSOLE environment variable (don't forget to write it back to flash).
If it doesn't boot then the easiest way is to fix a serial console to the machine and
change it, if you can't do that then use the ^c at an earlier point in the boot (before
the jump to bootstrap).
HTH
Adam






