you need to supply more information.  there is a stamped key number on the
lock - one as 250 key might not work on another (i think they go from
01 to 99).  there is also a `master' key which the service engineers have
which will open all within a series. they're pretty hard to get a hold of,
but it can be done ;-)

once you get the case open, it's pretty simple to disable the lock - remove
a nut and the internal latch mechanism and store it somewhere safe (taped
in a ziplock bag inside the machine?).

the case on the as250 is extremely tight anyway.


