> I have a Prime system here running RISC/OS and it's actually Sys3 R2 UNIX
> and nothing to do with Acorn.

A MIPStation is a workstation directly sold by MIPS with a MIPS processor (probably R3k
or R4k). It does run RISCOS, but not the one made by Acorn (that is for another
processor and in ROM). Acorn uses an ARM processor (Acorn machines are also called
Riscstations, not Mipstations). I believe the MIPStation has nothing to do with
Acorn... A MIPStation will also run NT 4.0 btw.

